1. Core Requirements & Technical Approach
Identity & Security Management:

Requirements: User registration, login, password reset, and profile updates.

Technical Implementation: ASP.NET Core Identity combined with JWT (JSON Web Tokens). We will implement a Refresh Token rotation strategy to ensure a seamless, secure user experience without abrupt session terminations.

Core Domain (Courses, Tasks & Notes):

Requirements: Create/edit/delete courses, manage tasks and their statuses, and create notes.

Technical Implementation: Standard RESTful APIs backed by Entity Framework Core (EF Core). We will strictly enforce a Soft Delete pattern (e.g., IsDeleted = true) for courses to prevent accidental cascading deletion of critical tasks and notes.

Data Aggregation (Dashboard):

Requirements: A unified view of all active courses and pending tasks.

Technical Implementation: A dedicated, read-only endpoint utilizing LINQ Projections. This ensures we fetch exactly what the client needs in a single database query, actively preventing the notorious N+1 query problem and eliminating data over-fetching.

External AI Service Integration:

Requirements: Transform raw, unstructured user notes into actionable, organized tasks.

Technical Implementation: Asynchronous API integration utilizing a lightweight, high-speed model like Gemini Flash 3.7. This ensures low-latency processing and prevents blocking the main server thread while handling AI requests.

